<title>UK: BT sees 50 mln stg less year redundancy costs.</title>
<headline>BT sees 50 mln stg less year redundancy costs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc said on Thursday it expected about 5,000 staff to leave the company during the year at a cost of around 350 million pounds -- 50 million pounds less than envisaged last November.</p>
<p>Over 4,000 staff left the company under voluntary redundancy terms in the first nine months of the year, at a cost of 274 million pounds.</p>
<p>Finance director Robert Brace told reporters that efficiency drives at the company's British operations would continue, but noted that new staff may be recruited internationally as the group expands abroad.</p>
<p>The company earlier reported that pretax profits in the third quarter rose to 909 million pounds from 829 million pounds -- after a 39 million stg redundancy charge.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7987</p>
